<figure class="diagram service-registry-map">
  <div class="registry-flow" aria-label="A native route header resolves its service slot through a static build table before selecting an endpoint">
    <div class="registry-node registry-header">
      <strong>Record header</strong>
      <span>direction <code>S→C</code><br>command <code>11</code><br>slot <code>5</code></span>
    </div>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <div class="registry-node registry-lookup">
      <strong>Static build table</strong>
      <span><code>slot 5 = Chat</code></span>
    </div>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <div class="registry-node registry-route">
      <strong>Dispatch key</strong>
      <span><code>(slot 5, command 11)</code></span>
    </div>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <div class="registry-node registry-endpoint">
      <strong>Endpoint</strong>
      <span><code>MessageRecv</code><br>payload decoder</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="chart-note">The wire contains slot <code>5</code>. Build-specific
  constants label the slot <code>Chat</code>. The inbound and outbound dispatch
